# 10. PURCHASE REQUISITION AGING – MANDATORY AND SEPARATE

PR aging is also mandatory.

It must be implemented independently from inventory stock aging.

Do not combine their calculation logic, configuration, reports or historical snapshots.

## 10.1 PR aging calculation

Calculate PR aging from the configured business event.

The default business reference should be the PR submission date for submitted transactions.

Draft PRs must not be incorrectly classified as pending approval.

Provide configurable alternative aging bases if the approved workflow requires them.

## 10.2 Example PR aging buckets

| PR Aging | Status |
|---|---|
| 0–3 days | Normal |
| 4–7 days | Attention |
| 8–15 days | Delayed |
| More than 15 days | Critical |

These thresholds must be configurable.

## 10.3 Configuration scope

- Company.
- Branch.
- Purchase Organization.
- PR Type.
- Approval Stage.
- Priority.

## 10.4 Display

- PR Number.
- PR Date.
- Submission Date.
- Current Status.
- Current Approval Owner.
- Days Pending.
- Aging Category.
- SLA Due Date, where configured.

Provide separate aging analysis for:

- Pending Manager Approval.
- Pending Department Approval.
- Pending Category Approval.
- Approved – Pending Buyer Assignment.
- Pending Buyer Action.
- Pending RFQ Conversion.
- Other configured PR workflow stages.

Do not mix completed or cancelled transactions with active pending aging unless a report explicitly requests historical aging.

